{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a1-explainer-about-popular-sweets-teach-gelato-from-italy-baklava-from-turkey-mochi-from-j/audio/main-9dda2dc13129.mp3","durationSec":156.072,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.04,"text":"We can ask four questions about a sweet."},{"start":2.62,"end":3.68,"text":"What ingredients are in it?"},{"start":3.84,"end":5,"text":"What form does it have?"},{"start":5.46,"end":6.6,"text":"How do people make it?"},{"start":6.94,"end":9.54,"text":"What is its texture, or how does it feel in your mouth?"},{"start":10.72,"end":13.12,"text":"Gelato is a popular frozen sweet from Italy."},{"start":13.72,"end":16.76,"text":"Its main ingredients are milk, sugar, and flavour."},{"start":16.76,"end":19.78,"text":"Gelato has less air than ice cream, so it is denser."},{"start":20.4,"end":23.68,"text":"Dense food is closely packed, not light and full of air."},{"start":24.6,"end":28.36,"text":"Baklava is a popular pastry sweet in Turkey and nearby countries."},{"start":28.36,"end":32.58,"text":"It has many thin layers of pastry with chopped nuts between them."},{"start":33.16,"end":36.28,"text":"Honey or sweet syrup goes over the pastry and soaks into it."},{"start":37.04,"end":40.06,"text":"“Soaks into” means the liquid enters the food."},{"start":40.9,"end":42.9,"text":"Baklava and gelato have very different forms."},{"start":43.48,"end":45.1,"text":"Gelato is one frozen mixture."},{"start":45.96,"end":49.64,"text":"Baklava is built from many pastry layers, nuts, and sweet liquid."},{"start":50.88,"end":53.04,"text":"Mochi is a popular rice cake from Japan."},{"start":53.88,"end":55.34,"text":"It is made from sticky rice."},{"start":55.34,"end":61.1,"text":"People pound the rice, or hit it again and again, until it becomes soft and stretchy."},{"start":61.42,"end":65.74,"text":"Mochi has a chewy texture, so you must move your teeth many times when you eat it."},{"start":66.1,"end":68.18,"text":"Some mochi has sweet bean paste inside."},{"start":68.66,"end":70.88,"text":"People can also eat it with other sweet toppings."},{"start":71.46,"end":74.68,"text":"Unlike layered baklava, mochi is a soft rice cake."},{"start":74.68,"end":78.74,"text":"A churro is a popular fried dough sweet from Spain."},{"start":79.56,"end":81.48,"text":"Frying means cooking food in hot oil."},{"start":81.86,"end":83.44,"text":"The dough cooks until it is golden."},{"start":84.04,"end":87.04,"text":"People often roll the churro in sugar after frying it."},{"start":87.56,"end":89.44,"text":"Churros are also eaten in Latin America."},{"start":90.12,"end":92.14,"text":"Some people eat them with thick hot chocolate."},{"start":92.82,"end":97.74,"text":"Their cooking method is different from gelato: churros go into hot oil, but gelato is frozen."},{"start":98.56,"end":102.66,"text":"An alfajor is a popular sweet in Argentina and other parts of South America."},{"start":103.28,"end":104.44,"text":"It is a sandwich cookie."},{"start":104.9,"end":108.98,"text":"Here, “sandwich” means that two round cookies hold a filling in the middle."},{"start":109.92,"end":111.62,"text":"The filling is a sweet milk caramel."},{"start":112.46,"end":115.6,"text":"Some alfajores also have chocolate or sugar on the outside."},{"start":116.66,"end":124.38,"text":"Their form is different from baklava: an alfajor has two cookies around one centre, while baklava has many thin pastry layers."},{"start":125.42,"end":126.68,"text":"Now use the four questions."},{"start":127.74,"end":129.78,"text":"Gelato is a dense, frozen milk sweet."},{"start":130.6,"end":133.02,"text":"Baklava is layered pastry with nuts and syrup."},{"start":133.92,"end":135.42,"text":"Mochi is a chewy rice cake."},{"start":136.14,"end":138.34,"text":"A churro is fried dough, often with sugar."},{"start":138.88,"end":141.52,"text":"An alfajor is a sandwich cookie with milk caramel."},{"start":142.44,"end":146.44,"text":"Their ingredients, forms, cooking methods, and textures make them different."},{"start":147.32,"end":155.56,"text":"One is frozen, one has many layers, one is chewy, one is fried, and one has two cookies around a filling."}],"words":[{"text":"We","start":0,"end":0.18},{"text":"can","start":0.18,"end":0.32},{"text":"ask","start":0.32,"end":0.58},{"text":"four","start":0.58,"end":0.92},{"text":"questions","start":0.92,"end":1.38},{"text":"about","start":1.38,"end":1.64},{"text":"a","start":1.64,"end":1.8},{"text":"sweet","start":1.8,"end":2.04},{"text":"What","start":2.62,"end":2.7},{"text":"ingredients","start":2.7,"end":3.06},{"text":"are","start":3.06,"end":3.36},{"text":"in","start":3.36,"end":3.5},{"text":"it","start":3.5,"end":3.68},{"text":"What","start":3.84,"end":4},{"text":"form","start":4,"end":4.38},{"text":"does","start":4.38,"end":4.58},{"text":"it","start":4.58,"end":4.72},{"text":"have","start":4.72,"end":5},{"text":"How","start":5.46,"end":5.7},{"text":"do","start":5.7,"end":5.88},{"text":"people","start":5.88,"end":6.1},{"text":"make","start":6.1,"end":6.34},{"text":"it","start":6.34,"end":6.6},{"text":"What","start":6.94,"end":7.1},{"text":"is","start":7.1,"end":7.24},{"text":"its","start":7.24,"end":7.44},{"text":"texture","start":7.44,"end":8},{"text":"or","start":8,"end":8.38},{"text":"how","start":8.38,"end":8.54},{"text":"does","start":8.54,"end":8.68},{"text":"it","start":8.68,"end":8.82},{"text":"feel","start":8.82,"end":9.02},{"text":"in","start":9.02,"end":9.16},{"text":"your","start":9.16,"end":9.26},{"text":"mouth","start":9.26,"end":9.54},{"text":"Gelato","start":10.72,"end":10.94},{"text":"is","start":10.94,"end":11.16},{"text":"a","start":11.16,"end":11.3},{"text":"popular","start":11.3,"end":11.8},{"text":"frozen","start":11.8,"end":12.18},{"text":"sweet","start":12.18,"end":12.58},{"text":"from","start":12.58,"end":12.8},{"text":"Italy","start":12.8,"end":13.12},{"text":"Its","start":13.72,"end":13.84},{"text":"main","start":13.84,"end":14.04},{"text":"ingredients","start":14.